{
  "_doc": {
    "about": "A todo's #tags read as the user's Gmail labels (shared/src/todos/label-tags.ts, Android :core todo/LabelTags.kt). Every case reads `labels`; only type \"user\" labels count.",
    "keys": "tagKey(in): lower case, each run of anything but letters, digits, marks and '_' as one '-', '-' and '_' trimmed from each '/' part, empty parts dropped. tag: labelTag(in), the key, or null when it has no letter.",
    "carried": "todoLabelIds(text): the ids of the labels the text's tags name, in tag order, each once; labels sharing a key are all named, in name order.",
    "color": "tagLabel(tag): the id of the first label (by name) the tag names, or null.",
    "suggest": "suggestTags(countTags(texts), own, prefix, limit ?? 5, labelTagNames(labels)): tags in use first, by use, then label tags no text uses, by key.",
    "rename": "renameTags(in, from, to): tags naming label `from` (or a label nested under it) rewritten for `to`.",
    "list": "labelTodos(todos, labelId): the ids of the todos whose tags name the label, in order.",
    "unlabeled": "unlabeledTags(texts, labels): the tags the texts use that name no label, one per key (the spelling most texts use, ignoring case, as first written; the first seen when tied), in key order, each with the label to make for it (the tag with empty / parts dropped, its longest leading run that names a label spelled as that label is); one whose label name a label has already (Gmail's own included, ignoring case) is left out.",
    "threads": "taggedThreadIds(threadIds, listed): the thread ids that listed lacks, each once, in order.",
    "filter": "taggedFilter(filter, labels): the filter with the user labels' ids dropped from requires."
  },
